************************************************************************ ToolPatch.ASM** * Copyright 1988-1989* Apple Computer, Inc.* All rights Reserved.** This file contains a jump table and jumps back into the regular code.* It is designed so that it can be linked to the object files that will* be linked in ROM.  Each manager that uses this mechanism will have* a subset of this code in its own source that is not linked to the ROM* so that the tool can be linked stand alone.*** Change History** 11 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Coding begins.***********************************************************************	Export ToolboxPatcher:EQUToolBoxPatcher	equ $E101BC*****************************************************************iToolboxPatcher	PROC EXPORT** This is the only entry point to this code.  The control* manager calls to this routine with the x-register set* to indicate what real call it wants to make.** In this way, the call can be patched.*** Inputs:*	x-reg    Call To Make** Outputs:*	no registers are altered.** External Refs:*	The real routines.** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	jmp (Table,x)Table	dc.w ToCMDispatcher	dc.w ToWMActivate	dc.w ToWMDeactivate	dc.w oopsToCMDispatcher		import RealCMDispatcher	jml RealCMDispatcherToWMActivate	import RealWMActivate	jml RealWMActivateToWMDeActivate	import RealWMDeActivate	jml RealWMDeActivateOops	brk 17	ENDP	END